{"findings":[{"id":"F-001","severity":"Critical","confidence":"high","title":"`proxyDeposit` can be farmed with zero amount to drain reward treasury","locations":["AaveBoost.sol:48","AaveBoost.sol:49","AaveBoost.sol:50"],"claim":"The reward branch is gated only by `aave.balanceOf(address(this)) >= REWARD` and does not enforce `amount > 0` or any per-user rate/accounting. Calling `proxyDeposit` with `amount = 0` still reaches `pool.deposit(..., amount + REWARD, ...)`, allowing repeated extraction of `REWARD` from contract-held AAVE.","impact":"Any account can repeatedly consume the subsidy and redirect deposits to itself, draining the contract's reward inventory and breaking incentive distribution.","paths":["Attacker calls `proxyDeposit(aave, attacker, 0)` while contract AAVE balance is at least `REWARD`.","`aave.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), 0)` succeeds with no economic cost.","`pool.deposit(aave, attacker, REWARD, false)` spends reward inventory.","Repeat until AAVE balance falls below `REWARD`."],"round":1,"source_agents":["codex_1","opencode_1"]},{"id":"F-002","severity":"High","confidence":"high","title":"Historical pools retain unlimited AAVE allowance after `setPool`","locations":["AaveBoost.sol:27","AaveBoost.sol:28","AaveBoost.sol:34","AaveBoost.sol:37"],"claim":"The contract grants `type(uint256).max` allowance to each configured pool via `safeIncreaseAllowance` but never revokes allowance from prior pools when rotating `pool`. Every previously configured pool keeps perpetual transfer rights over this contract’s AAVE.","impact":"If any previous pool address is compromised/malicious, it can drain all current and future AAVE held by this contract through `transferFrom`.","paths":["Deploy with pool P1, giving P1 max allowance on AAVE.","Owner calls `setPool(P2, ...)`; P2 also receives max allowance.","P1 allowance remains nonzero forever.","Compromised P1 transfers AAVE out of AaveBoost via `transferFrom`."],"round":1,"source_agents":["codex_1","opencode_1"]},{"id":"F-003","severity":"High","confidence":"medium","title":"`proxyDeposit` does not source the deposited `asset` from user, causing broken deposits and DoS paths","locations":["AaveBoost.sol:44","AaveBoost.sol:49","AaveBoost.sol:50","AaveBoost.sol:53"],"claim":"`proxyDeposit` only pulls `aave` from the caller in the reward branch and pulls nothing in the fallback branch; it never transfers `asset` from the caller. For pool implementations where `deposit` pulls `asset` from `msg.sender` (the AaveBoost contract), calls fail unless AaveBoost already holds and has approved that `asset`.","impact":"Proxy deposits can fail systematically (especially fallback path after rewards deplete), creating permissionless availability failure for intended user deposits.","paths":["User calls `proxyDeposit(asset, recipient, amount)` with `asset != aave`; contract still pulls AAVE (or nothing in fallback) instead of `asset`.","`pool.deposit(asset, ...)` attempts to source `asset` from AaveBoost, which is typically unfunded/unapproved for that token.","Call reverts; users cannot complete deposits via this proxy path.","After contract AAVE drops below `REWARD`, fallback branch (`pool.deposit` only) is broadly non-functional under the same funding assumption."],"round":1,"source_agents":["codex_1","opencode_1"]},{"id":"F-004","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","title":"`setPool` cannot update reward on same pool due max-allowance overflow in `safeIncreaseAllowance`","locations":["AaveBoost.sol:34","AaveBoost.sol:37","AaveBoost.sol:39"],"claim":"`setPool` always calls `aave.safeIncreaseAllowance(address(pool), maxUint)`. If current allowance is already max (constructor/previous call), adding max overflows and reverts under Solidity 0.8 checked arithmetic.","impact":"Owner cannot adjust `REWARD` while keeping the same pool address, reducing ability to operate/tune incentives and potentially blocking maintenance actions.","paths":["Pool already has max allowance from constructor or prior `setPool`.","Owner calls `setPool(existingPool, newReward)`.","Allowance increment `oldAllowance + maxUint` overflows and transaction reverts."],"round":1,"source_agents":["opencode_1"]},{"id":"F-005","severity":"Low","confidence":"medium","title":"`setPool` lacks zero/non-contract validation and can brick deposits if misconfigured","locations":["AaveBoost.sol:34","AaveBoost.sol:35","AaveBoost.sol:50","AaveBoost.sol:53"],"claim":"Unlike constructor checks, `setPool` does not validate `pool_ != address(0)` or contract code presence. Misconfiguration to an invalid target can make subsequent `proxyDeposit` calls revert when invoking `pool.deposit`.","impact":"A mistaken governance/operator action can halt all proxy deposits until corrected, causing service outage.","paths":["Owner sets `pool` to zero/non-contract via `setPool`.","Users call `proxyDeposit`.","External call to `pool.deposit` fails, reverting deposits globally."],"round":1,"source_agents":["codex_1","opencode_1"]}],"rejected_candidates":[{"title":"No withdrawal function — tokens permanently locked in the contract","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Not reliably true as a security issue in this design scope; locked-recovery behavior may be intentional, and owner can already redirect AAVE via pool-allowance control. More of design/governance policy than exploitable vulnerability."},{"title":"Owner can set malicious pool to drain all AAVE via infinite allowance","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Privileged-owner trust assumption, not a permissionless exploit. This is expected capability of `onlyOwner` and overlaps with governance risk rather than a standalone vulnerability."},{"title":"Unrestricted asset parameter allows draining any token held by the contract","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Contract only approves AAVE to pool; draining arbitrary tokens via `pool.deposit(asset,...)` is not generally feasible without corresponding allowance/funding and is unsupported by current code."},{"title":"Potential re-entrancy through pool.deposit call after AAVE transfer","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"No exploitable mutable state dependency was identified; claimed amplification is unnecessary because repeated direct calls already achieve reward draining."},{"title":"Missing events for all state-changing functions","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Observability issue only; no direct protocol-level fund-loss/theft/insolvency/DoS impact."},{"title":"No zero-address validation for recipient and asset in proxyDeposit","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Primarily caller-self-harm/input-sanity concern; no clear permissionless protocol exploit established from current code alone."},{"title":"REWARD uses uint128 but allowance and deposits operate on uint256","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"Type-width difference is intentional/benign under checked arithmetic and does not create a concrete exploit path."},{"title":"Pool address can be set to non-contract/zero, enabling user-fund capture without real deposit","source_agents":["codex_1","opencode_1"],"reason":"The specific fund-capture claim is overstated for Solidity 0.8.4 high-level external calls (invalid target reverts). Retained a downgraded misconfiguration-DoS variant instead."},{"title":"setPool does not validate that newReward_ is non-zero","source_agents":["opencode_1"],"reason":"`REWARD=0` is a parameter choice, not inherently exploitable; economic undesirability alone is governance/configuration policy, not a standalone vulnerability."}]}
